# Job Tracker — environment variable template
#
# This app stores ALL data locally in SQLite and makes NO external API calls.
# No environment variables are required to run the app.
#
# If you ever add external services (e.g. a sync API), follow this pattern:
#
#   1. Copy this file to .env.local  (never commit .env.local)
#   2. Set your values below
#   3. Access them in app code via expo-constants (see app.config.ts)
#
# .env.local is in .gitignore. .env.example is safe to commit — it has no real values.

# Example — uncomment and fill in if you add an API:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_KEY=your_key_here
